# MINIMAL REPRO (R40 Track D output-review, F1 — FIXED in R41 T-FMT-A) for
# `gg fmt` corrupting a COMMENT-ONLY file. This whole file is comments and
# nothing else, which is the entire point: with no items, the formatter emits
# no content before it flushes the comment sideband.
# Symptom was: the first comment got a spurious leading gap, and with >=2
# comments the first two were GLUED (the line break between them dropped):
#   printf '# a\n# b\n' | gg fmt   ->   "  # a# b"
# Intended (and now actual): a comment-only file round-trips BYTE-IDENTICALLY.
# Root: `Formatter::last_real_content_before` returned the SENTINEL 0 both for
# "content ends at byte 0" and for "no content at all", so `format`'s EOF
# trailing-comment hook treated the file's first comment as a trailing comment
# on a node that was never emitted. Fixed by making the empty case a distinct
# type (`Option<usize>`), so the trailing hook cannot fire before any content.
# The live guard is `fmt_comment_only_file_preserved` in tests/integration.rs,
# plus the corpus-wide `fmt_idempotent` sweep, which enumerates top-level
# fixtures and therefore covers this file now that it lives here.
#
# It used to sit in `known_gaps/` on the theory that a `main`-less file would
# register a runtime-parity non-MATCH. Measured: `gg run` on this file exits 1
# CLEANLY, and a clean non-zero oracle exit classifies as
# `RuntimeParityOutcome::RustRejected`, which the parity scan excludes from its
# denominator. Promotion is ceiling-neutral.
